From: Tushar Ganatra <tganatra@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 22:45:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ipsec: avoid double accounting inline output lifetime

The hybrid transform record counts the host-submitted first packet and
subsequent PPE-forwarded packets.  eip_ipsec_xfrm_account_output() also
added that first packet directly to the XFRM lifetime, then the periodic
transform record synchronization added it a second time.  This can expire
an inline SA early.

Keep state, expiry and replay validation for every host submission.  Leave
packet and byte lifetime accounting entirely to hardware for inline SAs;
host-only SAs continue to use software accounting.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/tree/10a89a95f814cd325e23105f102428644f45014f
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/8810d6098f75a5a6f38dc539e29cd7cfef760c78
Signed-off-by: Tushar Ganatra <tganatra@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
--- a/clients/ipsec/eip_ipsec_xfrm.c
+++ b/clients/ipsec/eip_ipsec_xfrm.c
@@ -105,6 +105,8 @@ static int eip_ipsec_xfrm_account_output(
 					 struct xfrm_state *xs,
 					 struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
+	struct net_device *dev = READ_ONCE(xs->data);
+	bool inline_offload;
 	int err = 0;
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&xs->lock);
@@ -126,8 +128,12 @@ static int eip_ipsec_xfrm_account_output(
 		goto unlock;
 	}
 
-	xs->curlft.bytes += skb->len;
-	xs->curlft.packets++;
+	inline_offload = eip_ipsec_sa_is_inline_xs(dev, xs);
+	if (!inline_offload) {
+		xs->curlft.bytes += skb->len;
+		xs->curlft.packets++;
+	}
+
 	xs->lastused = ktime_get_real_seconds();
 
 unlock:
